#X text 81 28 TRIGGERS: \; bang: trigger at full velocity (centered) \; float: trigger with velocity (0.0 - 1.0) \, centered \; list<f \, f>: trigger with velocity (0 - 1.0) and panning (values from -1 to 1 \, where -1 = full L \, 0 = centered \, 1 = full R. any value in between that range will balance both channels accordingly ) \; \; stop: stop playback \; file <s>: load audio file referenced by absolute path \; start <f>: set the start position offset \; end <f>: set the end position offset \; env_shape <f>: this is essentially the length of the envelope HOLD stage. for an AD envelope \, set the value to 0 Value greater than 0 result in a AHD envelope \, with the length of the HOLD stage increasing as the value of this parameter increases \; \; VELOCITY RESPONSE: \; vel_amp <f>: set how much the amplitude is scaled by velocity (the higher the value \, the lower the ampitude on lower velocities) \; vel_tone <f>: set how much the LP filter cutoff is affected by velocity (the higher this value \, the duller it sounds on low velocities) \; vel_start <f>: set how much the playback start position is offset by velocity (the higher this value \, the greater the start offset on low velocities) \; vel_attack <f>: set how much the ATTACK stage of the envelope is affected by velocity (the higher this value \, the longer the attack stage on lower velocities) \; vel_length <f>: set how much the length of the whole envelope is affected by velocity (the higher this value \, the shorter the duration of the envelope on lower velocities \;, f 143;
